01:03:22.980 --> 01:03:26.810
or hate on them anymore because
it's giving them access...

01:03:26.810 --> 01:03:28.900
I mean, they wouldn't have the ability,

01:03:28.900 --> 01:03:29.733
I don't think.

01:03:29.733 --> 01:03:31.490
You still have to do some work.

01:03:31.490 --> 01:03:32.640
No, not really.

01:03:32.640 --> 01:03:34.750
Yes, you have to pedal a little bit.

01:03:34.750 --> 01:03:38.630
But let me tell you, they're
not even breaking a sweat, man.

01:03:38.630 --> 01:03:39.630
It's funny-

01:03:39.630 --> 01:03:42.870
You pedal, but no, not really.

01:03:42.870 --> 01:03:45.130
This explains why I saw...

01:03:45.130 --> 01:03:47.720
When Shepherd and I were
hiking up a mountain recently

01:03:47.720 --> 01:03:49.090
on a fire road

01:03:49.090 --> 01:03:49.923
and we saw-
Oh gosh.

01:03:49.923 --> 01:03:51.482
Trucking.

01:03:51.482 --> 01:03:53.180
Well, he was stopped.

01:03:53.180 --> 01:03:57.130
He was stopped and drinking
water, but he was old.

01:03:57.130 --> 01:03:57.963
And I was like,

01:03:57.963 --> 01:03:59.690
"How the hell is this guy
getting up this mountain?"

01:03:59.690 --> 01:04:00.860
He must have had an e-bike."
E-bike.

01:04:00.860 --> 01:04:01.693
Yeah.

01:04:01.693 --> 01:04:05.160
And there will come a day

01:04:05.160 --> 01:04:06.610
when I will get one of those.

01:04:07.470 --> 01:04:09.420
But I just can't allow myself to do it now

01:04:09.420 --> 01:04:12.380
'cause that's what's keeping me in shape,

01:04:12.380 --> 01:04:15.780
is not allowing myself
to get one of those.

01:04:15.780 --> 01:04:16.980
Well, and you know what, you could get-

01:04:16.980 --> 01:04:18.950
But I'm jealous that they're
experiencing that, but-

01:04:18.950 --> 01:04:19.810
They also probably...

01:04:19.810 --> 01:04:21.510
You don't have to use it the whole time

01:04:21.510 --> 01:04:22.650
if you have like a standard-

01:04:22.650 --> 01:04:23.680
Yes, but that...

01:04:23.680 --> 01:04:24.627
There's no way.

01:04:25.500 --> 01:04:28.800
You're sitting there
trudging in granny gear

01:04:28.800 --> 01:04:31.860
knowing that you could zip
right on up the mountain?

01:04:31.860 --> 01:04:33.773
No, it would never happen.

01:04:34.730 --> 01:04:37.410
It's funny that we're
jealous of old people.

01:04:37.410 --> 01:04:39.253
Everybody on our list is old people,

01:04:40.270 --> 01:04:41.240
older than us.

01:04:41.240 --> 01:04:42.240
Give me another one.

01:04:43.820 --> 01:04:44.993
She is older.

01:04:45.900 --> 01:04:48.943
Marina O'Loughlin, no relation.

01:04:51.810 --> 01:04:54.650
Before this exercise, you
did not know these people.

01:04:54.650 --> 01:04:55.483
Yeah, well-

01:04:55.483 --> 01:04:56.920
Like, you used this as an occasion

01:04:56.920 --> 01:04:58.560
to come up with people.

01:04:58.560 --> 01:05:00.590
Well, let me say why.

01:05:00.590 --> 01:05:01.753
She's a food critic.

01:05:03.030 --> 01:05:03.873
Okay.

01:05:03.873 --> 01:05:06.860
And she's number four on my list,

01:05:06.860 --> 01:05:09.410
if it gives you any idea of
how important this is to me.

01:05:09.410 --> 01:05:11.640
Someone that you just
Googled on the internet,

01:05:11.640 --> 01:05:13.531
but food critic is really
what you're going for.

01:05:13.531 --> 01:05:16.550
And the reason that I
did not know about her...

01:05:16.550 --> 01:05:17.383
Well, first of all,

01:05:17.383 --> 01:05:20.000
it's not like I'm up on
the world of food critics.

01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:23.210
But also while she is a very
accomplished food critic,

01:05:23.210 --> 01:05:25.703
she's known for her anonymity.

01:05:26.900 --> 01:05:28.023
So she's not like...

01:05:28.023 --> 01:05:29.107
When I started looking, I was like,

01:05:29.107 --> 01:05:30.650
"I wanna find a food critic on my list,"

01:05:30.650 --> 01:05:34.200
because I've always loved the idea

01:05:34.200 --> 01:05:37.460
of just being someone
who gets paid to eat,

01:05:37.460 --> 01:05:38.760
which is, again, yes,

01:05:38.760 --> 01:05:40.380
I kind of do that already.

01:05:40.380 --> 01:05:41.400
Yeah, you do that already.

01:05:41.400 --> 01:05:43.080
But it's not the same.

01:05:43.080 --> 01:05:45.700
I'm not eating at a fine
dining establishment

01:05:45.700 --> 01:05:48.810
and then giving you my
refined opinion on it.

01:05:48.810 --> 01:05:50.560
Well, don't let the
Mythical Kitchen hear that.

01:05:50.560 --> 01:05:51.723
And also,

01:05:53.650 --> 01:05:56.800
she has not positioned
herself as a personality

01:05:56.800 --> 01:05:59.570
because she kinda talks
about the fact that...

01:06:00.428 --> 01:06:01.720
These people who...

01:06:01.720 --> 01:06:02.680
If you look up food critics,

01:06:02.680 --> 01:06:03.513
most of them like, oh,

01:06:03.513 --> 01:06:04.640
and they have this TV show,

01:06:04.640 --> 01:06:06.540
and they have this show that they're on,

01:06:06.540 --> 01:06:08.570
or they're a judge on this thing.

01:06:08.570 --> 01:06:10.040
She's kind of avoided that

01:06:10.040 --> 01:06:11.570
because she wants to maintain her...

01:06:11.570 --> 01:06:13.530
Even though you can find
out what she looks like

01:06:13.530 --> 01:06:15.030
and people do know who she is,

01:06:16.400 --> 01:06:21.270
but she's got anonymity when
it comes to the restaurants,

01:06:21.270 --> 01:06:25.200
but she has anonymity when
it comes to the public,

01:06:25.200 --> 01:06:26.990
which as a restaurant critic,

01:06:26.990 --> 01:06:30.230
you probably eat by yourself quite a bit.

01:06:30.230 --> 01:06:32.060
I've always been very resistant

01:06:32.060 --> 01:06:34.930
about eating in a restaurant by myself

01:06:34.930 --> 01:06:37.190
or going to a movie by myself because-

01:06:37.190 --> 01:06:38.140
Movie's easier.

01:06:38.140 --> 01:06:40.080
I don't think I've ever
been to a restaurant alone.

01:06:40.080 --> 01:06:42.150
But like my wife went on a solo trip

01:06:43.394 --> 01:06:44.480
a couple years ago

01:06:44.480 --> 01:06:47.180
and she just went to restaurants
by herself, you know?

01:06:49.040 --> 01:06:53.700
But I'm self-conscious of it
because I'm like, "Well..."

01:06:53.700 --> 01:06:57.040
It's fine if I just tell
the waiter I'm here alone,

01:06:57.040 --> 01:06:58.537
but then there's this
part of me that's like,

01:06:58.537 --> 01:07:01.824
"Yeah, but if you know
who I am, then it's like,

01:07:01.824 --> 01:07:04.040
'Oh right, he just eats by
himself because he's camp,

01:07:04.040 --> 01:07:04.900
he doesn't have any friends.'"

01:07:04.900 --> 01:07:07.130
So you're jealous of
being able to eat alone

01:07:07.130 --> 01:07:09.030
without being judged for it?

01:07:09.030 --> 01:07:10.660
Well, that's one aspect of it.

01:07:10.660 --> 01:07:13.480
But also if you just look at
the articles that she writes,

01:07:13.480 --> 01:07:17.793
I think she's with "The Times" in England.

01:07:19.290 --> 01:07:21.510
But she doesn't just...

01:07:21.510 --> 01:07:22.343
She'll go like,

01:07:22.343 --> 01:07:25.450
"I'm reviewing this hotel
that has a restaurant.

01:07:25.450 --> 01:07:27.116
I'm reviewing the hotel
and the restaurant,"

01:07:27.116 --> 01:07:30.550
and there's this like posh
hotel somewhere in Wales

01:07:30.550 --> 01:07:31.900
and she's writing about it.

01:07:33.400 --> 01:07:34.763
So she gets to travel.

01:07:35.660 --> 01:07:37.470
To travel nice places,

01:07:37.470 --> 01:07:39.050
to stay in nice places,

01:07:39.050 --> 01:07:42.800
to eat nice food is a very appealing thing

01:07:42.800 --> 01:07:43.820
that I like to...

01:07:43.820 --> 01:07:45.690
I like to do those things.

01:07:45.690 --> 01:07:49.100
But do you like to redeem
the travel by writing?

01:07:49.100 --> 01:07:51.080
I think you're onto something here.

01:07:51.080 --> 01:07:54.550
You wanna travel with
a purpose of writing.

01:07:54.550 --> 01:07:55.657
Second time it's come up.

01:07:55.657 --> 01:07:56.520
And you wanna eat.

01:07:56.520 --> 01:07:59.960
There's definitely something to...

01:07:59.960 --> 01:08:02.360
For me, when I experience something,

01:08:02.360 --> 01:08:04.070
I am compelled to write about it

01:08:04.070 --> 01:08:09.070
because it helps me to
understand it better for myself.

01:08:10.331 --> 01:08:11.164
You know what I'm saying?

01:08:11.164 --> 01:08:12.711
It's like when you have this experience

01:08:12.711 --> 01:08:14.030
and you're like, "I'm gonna
put this in my journal,"

01:08:14.030 --> 01:08:17.610
not so that somebody
can necessarily read it

01:08:17.610 --> 01:08:20.650
but it helps me understand
what happened to me

01:08:20.650 --> 01:08:21.590
and understand...

01:08:21.590 --> 01:08:22.673
And remember,

01:08:24.470 --> 01:08:27.520
I have this list in my Evernote

01:08:27.520 --> 01:08:29.333
which is like things I like,

01:08:30.502 --> 01:08:32.530
and I haven't added to it for a long time

01:08:32.530 --> 01:08:34.730
but it's just I wanna remember
that this restaurant was good

01:08:34.730 --> 01:08:37.750
or I wanna remember that this place

01:08:37.750 --> 01:08:39.610
was a really fun place to go.

01:08:39.610 --> 01:08:42.470
There's something about
cataloging that that is important,

01:08:42.470 --> 01:08:44.690
but also it's just the lifestyle.

01:08:44.690 --> 01:08:46.820
You know what you should do?

01:08:46.820 --> 01:08:50.643
You should commit yourself
to being a Yelp writer.

01:08:51.950 --> 01:08:56.070
That's a perfect journal,
it can be anonymous,

01:08:56.070 --> 01:08:58.090
where you can have...

01:08:58.090 --> 01:09:00.950
I'm sure you can look at your own account

01:09:00.950 --> 01:09:03.420
and have a record of
everywhere you've eaten

01:09:03.420 --> 01:09:05.630
and just a little something
that you've said about it.

01:09:05.630 --> 01:09:06.463
Don't write it...

01:09:06.463 --> 01:09:07.870
Don't do it for other people;

01:09:07.870 --> 01:09:09.600
I mean, they'll benefit from it;

01:09:09.600 --> 01:09:12.563
but maybe you'll start to get
notice because of your prose.

01:09:14.164 --> 01:09:15.740
I don't know.
Anonymously.

01:09:15.740 --> 01:09:17.560
Come on, man. Think about it.

01:09:17.560 --> 01:09:18.530
Don't poo poo it.

01:09:18.530 --> 01:09:19.527
Don't make the stink face.

01:09:19.527 --> 01:09:20.397
This is a good idea.

01:09:20.397 --> 01:09:24.954
I think that I want to write in a more-

01:09:24.954 --> 01:09:27.830
You want the cred.

01:09:27.830 --> 01:09:29.023
No, no, that's not what...

01:09:29.023 --> 01:09:30.610
I mean, yeah, I do want cred,

01:09:30.610 --> 01:09:32.959
but that's what I'm jealous about.

01:09:32.959 --> 01:09:33.950
But you could still get it.

01:09:33.950 --> 01:09:38.190
I mean, people get cred
from writing Amazon reviews.

01:09:38.190 --> 01:09:39.440
It's a different style.

01:09:40.360 --> 01:09:41.810
It's a different style, though.

01:09:41.810 --> 01:09:42.700
You could be the first.

01:09:42.700 --> 01:09:44.200
It's not experiential.

01:09:44.200 --> 01:09:45.260
Make it experiential.

01:09:45.260 --> 01:09:50.110
It's like, "We had the
Hawaiian shrimp combo."

01:09:50.110 --> 01:09:51.467
No, there are more-

01:09:51.467 --> 01:09:54.357
"Everyone at my table ordered, so..."

01:09:54.357 --> 01:09:55.190
I don't...

01:09:55.190 --> 01:09:56.023
It's-
No,

01:09:56.023 --> 01:09:58.473
there are people who write
reviews in a different way.

01:09:59.540 --> 01:10:00.520
You could do it your way.

01:10:00.520 --> 01:10:01.353
You think there's somebody who's-

01:10:01.353 --> 01:10:03.600
And you have a record of
everywhere that you've eaten,

01:10:03.600 --> 01:10:04.433
and it gives you...

01:10:04.433 --> 01:10:05.540
It's like, "Well, I
gotta eat somewhere else

01:10:05.540 --> 01:10:06.930
'cause I gotta write about it-
You think there's somebody

01:10:06.930 --> 01:10:09.170
who wrote Yelp reviews-
"They're counting on me."

01:10:09.170 --> 01:10:11.820
And then transitioned into
full-time food critic?

01:10:11.820 --> 01:10:13.490
Is that what you want?

01:10:13.490 --> 01:10:15.080
No, I'm just saying
that I just don't think

01:10:15.080 --> 01:10:16.230
that bridge gets there.

01:10:16.230 --> 01:10:17.670
Is that what you want?

01:10:17.670 --> 01:10:20.303
No, but if I'm gonna write the reviews,

01:10:21.690 --> 01:10:24.080
I wanna be able to approach
it as a food critic

01:10:24.080 --> 01:10:25.407
not as just a Yelper.

01:10:26.613 --> 01:10:28.690
It just feels like a
distinctly different exercise.

01:10:28.690 --> 01:10:30.970
Well, that's your only path.

01:10:30.970 --> 01:10:32.780
I mean, you need a portfolio.

01:10:32.780 --> 01:10:35.660
I think I'm just gonna keep
eating at good restaurants

01:10:35.660 --> 01:10:37.510
and maybe start eating at them alone.

01:10:40.340 --> 01:10:41.240
I only have what?

01:10:41.240 --> 01:10:42.073
Two more?

01:10:42.920 --> 01:10:44.230
This one right here...

01:10:44.230 --> 01:10:45.187
Again, it's another older person.

01:10:45.187 --> 01:10:46.860
Two more? I'm about...

01:10:46.860 --> 01:10:47.970
I just gave you my number four,

01:10:47.970 --> 01:10:48.810
so I have three more.

01:10:48.810 --> 01:10:50.943
Oh, maybe I'm cutting ones.

01:10:52.960 --> 01:10:54.803
This guy's 49 years old,

01:10:55.951 --> 01:10:59.850
but he, ever since, like for decades,

01:10:59.850 --> 01:11:04.850
he has been a prolific music producer.

01:11:05.050 --> 01:11:10.050
And this one's much more
squarely inspirational

01:11:10.830 --> 01:11:12.420
than it is jealous.

01:11:12.420 --> 01:11:14.410
I actually don't know

01:11:14.410 --> 01:11:19.090
exactly what I'm jealous
of Pharrell about,

01:11:19.090 --> 01:11:21.713
but I think I can start
to put my finger on it.

01:11:23.630 --> 01:11:27.100
The dude, for decades,

01:11:27.100 --> 01:11:29.740
has been creating music, producing music,

01:11:29.740 --> 01:11:32.140
showing up in all types of places;

01:11:32.140 --> 01:11:36.150
of course, with the Neptunes
back in the day, but then...

01:11:36.150 --> 01:11:36.983
I mean,

01:11:39.000 --> 01:11:40.350
at his age,

01:11:40.350 --> 01:11:45.350
he's still producing for the
top artist on the planet.

01:11:47.280 --> 01:11:50.240
Like the new Kendrick album,

01:11:50.240 --> 01:11:53.340
he produced "Mr. Morale,"

01:11:53.340 --> 01:11:55.590
that's the only song he produced on there.

01:11:55.590 --> 01:11:58.710
But to be on that album, which is like...

01:11:58.710 --> 01:12:03.370
You know, it's like a
treasure, a time capsule,

01:12:03.370 --> 01:12:06.130
it's like this artistic expression

01:12:06.130 --> 01:12:08.870
is something that will
always be referred to

01:12:08.870 --> 01:12:10.193
not just in hip hop,

01:12:11.170 --> 01:12:14.026
whether you go back and listen
to it all the time or not,

01:12:14.026 --> 01:12:16.400
it's just you can't deny it.

01:12:16.400 --> 01:12:18.470
The fact that he's working with Kendrick,

01:12:18.470 --> 01:12:19.500
he's working with...

01:12:20.340 --> 01:12:22.540
And he's singing the hook

01:12:22.540 --> 01:12:27.350
on the Pusha T album,

01:12:27.350 --> 01:12:28.610
which I really like.

01:12:28.610 --> 01:12:30.140
So it's like...

01:12:30.140 --> 01:12:33.930
And he actually sang
the hook on "Alright,"

01:12:33.930 --> 01:12:37.790
the Kendrick song from
"To Pimp a Butterfly."

01:12:37.790 --> 01:12:41.210
So he's been around, he's in the mix,

01:12:41.210 --> 01:12:43.740
and he's getting older.

01:12:43.740 --> 01:12:44.830
First of all, he doesn't-

01:12:44.830 --> 01:12:46.293
He doesn't look 49.
He look like a...

01:12:46.293 --> 01:12:49.407
I mean, he looks so young
but he's staying young.

01:12:49.407 --> 01:12:52.130
Again, I think this is
more of an inspiration.

01:12:52.130 --> 01:12:53.790
But the thing that I'm jealous of

01:12:53.790 --> 01:12:58.670
is that he's in the world
with these musicians

01:12:58.670 --> 01:13:01.230
and artists that are
the top of their game,

01:13:01.230 --> 01:13:02.540
he's rubbing shoulders with them,

01:13:02.540 --> 01:13:04.240
he's creating with them.

01:13:04.240 --> 01:13:05.780
So he's not just a fly on the wall

01:13:05.780 --> 01:13:08.150
but he's in the mix,

01:13:08.150 --> 01:13:09.310
and that's just like...

01:13:09.310 --> 01:13:11.740
It's a world that's so fascinating to me,

01:13:11.740 --> 01:13:14.040
and I just love the idea of it.

01:13:14.040 --> 01:13:15.840
So I'm jealous that this guy gets to walk

01:13:15.840 --> 01:13:17.020
into a room and...

01:13:18.230 --> 01:13:21.620
If Prince were alive, he'd
go up and talk to him,

01:13:21.620 --> 01:13:22.453
you know?

01:13:22.453 --> 01:13:26.560
He was in that Kanye documentary.

01:13:26.560 --> 01:13:27.393
Right.

01:13:27.393 --> 01:13:28.673
Like, in the early days of Kanye.

01:13:29.750 --> 01:13:30.583
Yeah.

01:13:30.583 --> 01:13:31.416
And there's that scene

01:13:31.416 --> 01:13:34.907
where he recognizes Kanye's talent,

01:13:34.907 --> 01:13:37.840
and he was like no one was
expecting it at the time.

01:13:37.840 --> 01:13:38.673
Right.

01:13:38.673 --> 01:13:40.970
And he looked exactly
the same as he does now.

01:13:40.970 --> 01:13:41.803
Yeah.

01:13:41.803 --> 01:13:42.660
It's just so weird.

01:13:42.660 --> 01:13:43.610
Yeah.

01:13:43.610 --> 01:13:44.443
He'd be a cool guy to meet him.

01:13:44.443 --> 01:13:46.080
I have a music producer in my top three,

01:13:46.080 --> 01:13:47.430
but I he's not my number three,

01:13:47.430 --> 01:13:49.290
so I'm gonna give you my number three.

01:13:49.290 --> 01:13:50.890
Well, just do 'em outta order.

01:13:51.760 --> 01:13:52.593
Okay.

01:13:52.593 --> 01:13:54.610
Well, I'll give you my number two then.

01:13:54.610 --> 01:13:56.270
My number two is Rick Rubin.

01:13:56.270 --> 01:13:58.150
Oh yeah. Same thing.

01:13:58.150 --> 01:14:00.957
See, I got you to watch
that Paul McCartney thing,

01:14:00.957 --> 01:14:03.790
'cause you told me, the "3,2,1."

01:14:03.790 --> 01:14:04.630
And also,

01:14:04.630 --> 01:14:07.950
even though he doesn't
actually cameo in it,

01:14:07.950 --> 01:14:10.687
in the second season of "Dave,"

01:14:12.840 --> 01:14:15.680
there's like the Rick Rubin episode.

01:14:15.680 --> 01:14:16.880
I don't remember that.

01:14:18.150 --> 01:14:19.010
Wasn't that "Dave?"

01:14:19.010 --> 01:14:20.460
I think fell off.

01:14:20.460 --> 01:14:22.963
I didn't finish Dave
season two for some reason.

01:14:23.870 --> 01:14:25.643
Really?
I gotta finish that.

01:14:27.330 --> 01:14:29.390
I think that's the show that I saw it on.

01:14:29.390 --> 01:14:33.343
So what about him makes you jealous?

01:14:34.410 --> 01:14:35.243
Well,

01:14:36.400 --> 01:14:40.620
