and to build a company

01:26:17.820 --> 01:26:22.820
has involved quite a bit
of giving of ourselves,

01:26:23.700 --> 01:26:27.930
not just our time but
literally giving of ourselves.

01:26:27.930 --> 01:26:31.810
Words that come out of our
mouths and go on the internet,

01:26:31.810 --> 01:26:36.730
there's so much that we're
putting out there of ourselves;

01:26:36.730 --> 01:26:39.093
on this podcast, being vulnerable, right?

01:26:40.037 --> 01:26:40.870
And

01:26:43.970 --> 01:26:47.240
it was almost like when you take "Inside,"

01:26:47.240 --> 01:26:50.180
Bo Burnham hasn't been saying
anything on social media,

01:26:50.180 --> 01:26:52.183
he doesn't say anything on Twitter,

01:26:53.800 --> 01:26:55.210
he doesn't have a podcast,

01:26:55.210 --> 01:26:58.000
he's not constantly talking about himself

01:26:58.000 --> 01:26:59.623
and what he thinks, right?

01:27:00.870 --> 01:27:04.150
But then he bottles all that up

01:27:04.150 --> 01:27:07.150
and puts it into this hour long special

01:27:07.150 --> 01:27:07.983
that is like,

01:27:07.983 --> 01:27:09.920
"This is what I've been thinking.

01:27:09.920 --> 01:27:11.680
These are my thoughts,"

01:27:11.680 --> 01:27:13.660
not given to you in this steady stream

01:27:13.660 --> 01:27:16.230
where you can't escape me
by going on the internet,

01:27:16.230 --> 01:27:17.063
but like,

01:27:17.063 --> 01:27:20.710
"If you wanna tune into this
fire hydrant of expression

01:27:20.710 --> 01:27:22.800
and creativity and vulnerability,

01:27:22.800 --> 01:27:24.950
it's in this special
that I've been working on

01:27:24.950 --> 01:27:26.450
for this length of time.

01:27:26.450 --> 01:27:28.120
And now I'm working on this other thing,

01:27:28.120 --> 01:27:28.953
and you know what,

01:27:28.953 --> 01:27:29.870
you'll be around for...

01:27:29.870 --> 01:27:32.860
And I don't have to stay on your radar

01:27:32.860 --> 01:27:34.770
with every little piece of
content that I put out."

01:27:34.770 --> 01:27:36.020
I'm jealous of that.

01:27:36.020 --> 01:27:39.280
I'm jealous that somebody
can be so prolific

01:27:39.280 --> 01:27:40.113
yet

01:27:41.440 --> 01:27:45.950
not have some so much
volume in their output.

01:27:45.950 --> 01:27:49.123
Before you give your number one,

01:27:50.670 --> 01:27:52.690
do you think that this has been

01:27:55.030 --> 01:27:58.820
a positive experience for
us to have this discussion?

01:27:58.820 --> 01:28:01.450
Like, I was more worked
up at the beginning,

01:28:01.450 --> 01:28:03.950
you brow's a little
crinkled at this point.

01:28:03.950 --> 01:28:06.237
Do you feel like we're
getting things out there

01:28:06.237 --> 01:28:10.483
and that it's cathartic or
that it's fomenting something?

01:28:12.970 --> 01:28:14.880
I think those are the same.

01:28:14.880 --> 01:28:18.363
So I think that if you have a frustration,

01:28:19.780 --> 01:28:20.820
by taking it out,

01:28:20.820 --> 01:28:22.637
looking at it and expressing it...

01:28:22.637 --> 01:28:24.270
I mean, this is what I
do in therapy, right?

01:28:24.270 --> 01:28:25.870
I'm assuming this is what
you do in therapy as well.

01:28:25.870 --> 01:28:28.913
If there's something that
is on your mind in this way,

01:28:29.970 --> 01:28:34.710
I think that it is only
good to vocalize it

01:28:34.710 --> 01:28:36.350
and actually examine it.

01:28:36.350 --> 01:28:41.350
So ultimately, yes, very positive,

01:28:41.580 --> 01:28:42.537
but it may not be like,

01:28:42.537 --> 01:28:45.410
"Oh, this is gonna put me
in a good mood right now,"

01:28:45.410 --> 01:28:46.910
but that's not how I'm gonna judge

01:28:46.910 --> 01:28:48.710
whether or not it is a net positive.

01:28:50.710 --> 01:28:51.860
You know me,

01:28:51.860 --> 01:28:54.470
I get very creatively frustrated, right?

01:28:54.470 --> 01:28:59.470
Because of I'm extremely
grateful for all the success

01:28:59.570 --> 01:29:00.890
and the things that work,

01:29:00.890 --> 01:29:02.847
but I'm also frustrated
that we can't just be like,

01:29:02.847 --> 01:29:05.917
"Let's just create this
aspirational thing,"

01:29:07.095 --> 01:29:08.497
and to be financed in the way

01:29:08.497 --> 01:29:10.737
that we want it to be
financed, and just like,

01:29:10.737 --> 01:29:12.330
"Here's this thing that we thought of

01:29:12.330 --> 01:29:13.887
and we spent all this time on."

01:29:16.685 --> 01:29:19.610
But for me, that desire's
not gonna go away.

01:29:19.610 --> 01:29:22.440
When I think about this list of people,

01:29:22.440 --> 01:29:23.273
it isn't like,

01:29:23.273 --> 01:29:25.640
"Oh man, I have regret
about choices we've made,"

01:29:25.640 --> 01:29:28.130
I just think, "I'm still very young,

01:29:28.130 --> 01:29:30.130
I have a lot of life left.

01:29:30.130 --> 01:29:33.323
And the way that I'm
going to position myself

01:29:35.430 --> 01:29:38.500
in the future is to get in the
way of more of these things

01:29:38.500 --> 01:29:40.240
that I admire in these people," right?

01:29:40.240 --> 01:29:43.160
You want to actually
engineer your life in a way

01:29:43.160 --> 01:29:46.060
where you move towards the
things that are inspiring.

01:29:46.060 --> 01:29:47.750
So it may be frustrating,

01:29:47.750 --> 01:29:49.030
but I think that that frustration

01:29:49.030 --> 01:29:51.090
is just us being honest about...

01:29:54.140 --> 01:29:58.840
I mean, I get tired of seeing
myself on the internet,

01:29:58.840 --> 01:30:00.393
to be perfectly frank about it.

01:30:02.160 --> 01:30:02.993
You know what I'm saying?

01:30:02.993 --> 01:30:04.567
It's just like,

01:30:04.567 --> 01:30:07.220
"I kind of wish I didn't
have to constantly be

01:30:07.220 --> 01:30:10.757
in multiple streams of content
in order for this to work."

01:30:12.300 --> 01:30:14.090
Bob Burnham doesn't have to do that.

01:30:14.090 --> 01:30:17.460
Bob Burnham doesn't have to
make an internet video today

01:30:17.460 --> 01:30:20.040
to be talked about and to be appreciated.

01:30:20.040 --> 01:30:20.873
And you may say,

01:30:20.873 --> 01:30:21.820
"Well, you guys don't have to either."

01:30:21.820 --> 01:30:23.360
And I'm not saying that I'm burned out

01:30:23.360 --> 01:30:24.193
or anything like that.

01:30:24.193 --> 01:30:26.337
I'm just saying that I'm jealous
of someone who can be like,

01:30:26.337 --> 01:30:28.880
"I'm gonna ball it all up and
give it to you in this way."

01:30:28.880 --> 01:30:31.730
That's not our business model.

01:30:31.730 --> 01:30:34.313
Our business model is
constant contact and content,

01:30:36.720 --> 01:30:39.590
and it works and people appreciate it,

01:30:39.590 --> 01:30:43.747
but I would be dishonest if I said,

01:30:43.747 --> 01:30:46.520
"Well, I'm jealous of the people
who don't have to do that,"

01:30:46.520 --> 01:30:50.203
which leads me to my
number one, Donald Glover,

01:30:52.160 --> 01:30:54.130
for all the same reasons

01:30:54.130 --> 01:30:58.330
but I think even more so
than Bo Burnham because-

01:30:58.330 --> 01:30:59.163
He does so many different things.

01:30:59.163 --> 01:31:00.720
He does so many different things.

01:31:00.720 --> 01:31:01.553
So you can be like,

01:31:01.553 --> 01:31:03.830
"I am going to become a musical artist.

01:31:03.830 --> 01:31:06.070
And I'm not just gonna
be a good musical artist,

01:31:06.070 --> 01:31:08.100
I'm gonna be a great musical artist.

01:31:08.100 --> 01:31:09.960
And I'm not just gonna be
a great musical artist,

01:31:09.960 --> 01:31:13.357
I'm gonna be a culture
defining musical artist,"

01:31:14.600 --> 01:31:16.610
in a way that every person

01:31:16.610 --> 01:31:19.080
who's doing only music aspires to

01:31:21.310 --> 01:31:22.200
is such a-

01:31:22.200 --> 01:31:23.620
Yeah, but then I'm gonna have this show

01:31:23.620 --> 01:31:27.030
that's like an artistic expression.

01:31:27.030 --> 01:31:27.863
Yeah.

01:31:27.863 --> 01:31:31.307
And I'm gonna make choices on
that show that are for him.

01:31:31.307 --> 01:31:32.760
Are you caught up?

01:31:32.760 --> 01:31:33.876
I'm not caught up on this season.

01:31:33.876 --> 01:31:35.520
I haven't started.

01:31:35.520 --> 01:31:38.173
I'm waiting for the right time to hit it.

01:31:40.160 --> 01:31:42.110
And then everything that I just said,

01:31:42.970 --> 01:31:44.140
he doesn't...

01:31:46.467 --> 01:31:50.740
"Oh, let's go watch Donald
Glover's Instagram story today."

01:31:50.740 --> 01:31:52.890
It doesn't exist

01:31:54.210 --> 01:31:56.403
because it doesn't need to.

01:31:56.403 --> 01:31:57.520
I mean, really,

01:31:57.520 --> 01:31:58.963
it's really a question like:

01:31:59.870 --> 01:32:01.670
Would you do-

01:32:01.670 --> 01:32:02.503
I mean, first of all,

01:32:02.503 --> 01:32:03.620
neither one of us are very active

01:32:03.620 --> 01:32:06.110
on social media to begin...

01:32:06.110 --> 01:32:08.600
but our presence on
social media is very high

01:32:08.600 --> 01:32:11.380
because the Mythical
presence is very high.

01:32:11.380 --> 01:32:15.800
But if you never had to tweet again,

01:32:15.800 --> 01:32:18.230
you never had to put your
opinion out about anything,

01:32:18.230 --> 01:32:20.250
you never had to say
where you stood on this,

01:32:20.250 --> 01:32:21.537
you never had to be,

01:32:21.537 --> 01:32:24.210
"Here's a picture of me
doing this," ever again,

01:32:24.210 --> 01:32:25.043
and you could just be like,

01:32:25.043 --> 01:32:26.850
"Here's the thing that I wanted to create

01:32:26.850 --> 01:32:28.730
and you guys can watch it if you want to,"

01:32:28.730 --> 01:32:29.830
would you choose that?

01:32:31.410 --> 01:32:35.240
Well, I feel like the only thing...

01:32:35.240 --> 01:32:36.803
I don't really tweet.

01:32:36.803 --> 01:32:40.020
I don't really share much.

01:32:40.020 --> 01:32:43.115
I've kind of hit a lull.

01:32:43.115 --> 01:32:45.860
There's been sometimes
when I'll get back into it,

01:32:45.860 --> 01:32:47.640
but the majority of the
time I'm not into it

01:32:47.640 --> 01:32:52.090
so then I just feel guilty
that I'm not doing enough

01:32:52.950 --> 01:32:55.310
from a professional standpoint.

01:32:55.310 --> 01:32:57.370
You're right.
So to me it's about...

01:32:58.661 --> 01:33:01.010
Like, it's an obligation
that I'm not fulfilling,

01:33:01.010 --> 01:33:04.363
so it's more about the
feeling of not fulfilling it.

01:33:07.510 --> 01:33:11.463
So I don't feel like I have to trade it.

01:33:13.310 --> 01:33:16.500
But in general, would at I trade...

01:33:16.500 --> 01:33:17.333
I don't know.

01:33:17.333 --> 01:33:22.150
I feel like would I trade
my experience right now

01:33:22.150 --> 01:33:24.813
for any of the people that I'm jealous of?

01:33:25.980 --> 01:33:29.850
And if you have to take a
kitten caboodle, I wouldn't.

01:33:29.850 --> 01:33:31.753
Yeah, I agree with that.

01:33:33.040 --> 01:33:35.778
I mean, I don't know any
of these people personally.

01:33:35.778 --> 01:33:36.611
You know?
Yeah.

01:33:36.611 --> 01:33:41.450
Again, I do read things in
the MrBeast profile piece,

01:33:41.450 --> 01:33:42.900
it's like, okay,

01:33:42.900 --> 01:33:45.944
it's like things about his existence

01:33:45.944 --> 01:33:48.453
are things that I'm not jealous of.

01:33:49.430 --> 01:33:51.990
It's like when you get into the specifics.

01:33:51.990 --> 01:33:54.500
I don't know Bo Burnham personally,

01:33:54.500 --> 01:33:57.177
I don't know what his
experience is, but like-

01:33:57.177 --> 01:34:00.235
But even his special came
from a place of pain.

01:34:00.235 --> 01:34:01.068
Right.

01:34:01.068 --> 01:34:01.901
So, yeah.

01:34:01.901 --> 01:34:02.734
I completely agree-
So it's like

01:34:02.734 --> 01:34:03.567
I don't want that.

01:34:03.567 --> 01:34:04.400
I'm not saying I want to be-
And I'm like, "Man,

01:34:04.400 --> 01:34:09.319
I'm in a pretty nice spot
and I'm pretty content."

01:34:09.319 --> 01:34:10.800
I'm actually...

01:34:10.800 --> 01:34:12.500
I'm jealous of aspects of things,

01:34:12.500 --> 01:34:14.800
but if you can't pick and choose

01:34:14.800 --> 01:34:15.810
then it's like there's no one

01:34:15.810 --> 01:34:18.030
that I would trade my life for.

01:34:18.030 --> 01:34:18.863
It's like-

01:34:18.863 --> 01:34:20.250
I completely agree with that.

01:34:20.250 --> 01:34:23.100
As a matter of fact, I was
telling Jessie about this.

01:34:23.100 --> 01:34:25.663
I know we're getting
long here, but who cares?

01:34:28.600 --> 01:34:30.070
I was telling her recently, I was like,

01:34:30.070 --> 01:34:33.028
and I was talking to my
therapist about this too.

01:34:33.028 --> 01:34:34.530
I was like...

01:34:34.530 --> 01:34:36.530
I haven't struggled with depression.

01:34:36.530 --> 01:34:37.363
There hasn't been...

01:34:37.363 --> 01:34:41.530
I mean, I get depressed at
times like anybody who gets sad

01:34:41.530 --> 01:34:43.090
or kind of gets down in
the dumps or whatever,

01:34:43.090 --> 01:34:46.550
but I haven't struggled
with it like a diagnosable-

01:34:46.550 --> 01:34:49.070
Well, yeah, I wouldn't call
those things depression then,

01:34:49.070 --> 01:34:49.920
but yeah, go ahead.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:34:49.920 --> 01:34:54.477
But I just was talking to
'em recently and I was like,

01:34:54.477 --> 01:34:56.560
"You know, I keep sort of...

01:34:56.560 --> 01:34:58.700
There's been multiple times
over the past couple of months

01:34:58.700 --> 01:35:00.970
where I'm just like, 'I'm happy.'"

01:35:02.070 --> 01:35:02.903
You know?

01:35:02.903 --> 01:35:05.261
And I tend to not be a
very satisfied person.

01:35:05.261 --> 01:35:09.610
I'm very, very driven,
like to a maniacal point,

01:35:09.610 --> 01:35:11.440
and I get a lot of satisfaction

01:35:11.440 --> 01:35:14.060
out of coming up with
something and then being...

01:35:14.060 --> 01:35:15.610
and then like, "I'm gonna go after that,"

01:35:15.610 --> 01:35:18.023
I'm geared to that.

01:35:18.860 --> 01:35:20.967
So there's not a lot of time
where I just stop and think,

01:35:20.967 --> 01:35:23.030
"Oh, I'm happy.

01:35:23.030 --> 01:35:25.070
I've got it really, really good."

01:35:25.070 --> 01:35:28.380
But there's just been a number
of times recently where...

01:35:28.380 --> 01:35:29.213
And I don't know

01:35:29.213 --> 01:35:32.460
if it's with Locke getting
ready to go to college

01:35:32.460 --> 01:35:35.070
and it's like our family
dynamic is about to change

01:35:35.070 --> 01:35:35.903
or whatever,

01:35:37.030 --> 01:35:38.970
but just kind of just
recognizing that like:

01:35:38.970 --> 01:35:42.180
Man, if there is a universe,

01:35:42.180 --> 01:35:43.770
if there are really multiple worlds

01:35:43.770 --> 01:35:45.420
and there's other versions of me out there

01:35:45.420 --> 01:35:47.730
who made other decisions
at different points

01:35:47.730 --> 01:35:49.770
and ended up in different places,

01:35:49.770 --> 01:35:54.570
I just can't imagine many of them

01:35:54.570 --> 01:35:56.357
being better than this.

01:35:56.357 --> 01:36:00.550
I recognize that how great
everything has worked out.

01:36:00.550 --> 01:36:02.200
So I completely,

01:36:02.200 --> 01:36:04.810
by talking about my
frustrations creatively

01:36:04.810 --> 01:36:06.630
and how I love the fact that Donald...

01:36:06.630 --> 01:36:08.260
I'm jealous of the fact that Donald Glover

01:36:08.260 --> 01:36:11.040
and Bo Burnham don't have to
have a social media presence

01:36:11.040 --> 01:36:12.440
because their creative presence

01:36:12.440 --> 01:36:15.120
is so overwhelmingly significant,

01:36:15.120 --> 01:36:16.800
I'm jealous of that,

01:36:16.800 --> 01:36:18.010
but I completely agree with you

01:36:18.010 --> 01:36:19.770
that I'm not saying I wanna trade places

01:36:19.770 --> 01:36:21.360
with anybody on the list.

01:36:21.360 --> 01:36:23.800
Yeah, I think that we have...

01:36:25.240 --> 01:36:26.073
I mean,

01:36:27.813 --> 01:36:29.773
we're enjoying success.

01:36:31.310 --> 01:36:35.180
We're at like a great point in our careers

01:36:35.180 --> 01:36:36.380
where there's things...

01:36:36.380 --> 01:36:39.150
there's the relationship with our fans

01:36:39.150 --> 01:36:42.922
and the relationships that
we have with each other,

01:36:42.922 --> 01:36:45.890
all of it is kind of
like we're in a good spot

01:36:46.850 --> 01:36:48.350
personally and professionally.

01:36:49.600 --> 01:36:51.960
I think another part of it is,

01:36:51.960 --> 01:36:54.670
if you focus on the professional part,

01:36:54.670 --> 01:36:59.670
we do have a lot of
freedom and power to say,

01:37:00.237 --> 01:37:01.790
"Okay, we can..."

01:37:01.790 --> 01:37:04.810
If there's anything we want
to go after or restructure,

01:37:04.810 --> 01:37:06.810
or anything that we wanna do,

01:37:06.810 --> 01:37:11.250
it's like we have the ability to do that.

01:37:11.250 --> 01:37:14.560
Well, we don't have the ability
to do anything we wanna do

01:37:14.560 --> 01:37:15.393
and have...

01:37:15.393 --> 01:37:19.000
like to work with any actor we want

01:37:19.000 --> 01:37:21.830
or to get any film we want made

01:37:21.830 --> 01:37:26.290
or to stretch our legs
creatively in any way possible,

01:37:26.290 --> 01:37:31.290
but compared to most people
in an artistic field,

01:37:31.860 --> 01:37:33.430
we have so many more options

01:37:33.430 --> 01:37:36.650
and so much more power

01:37:36.650 --> 01:37:41.130
to orchestrate our lives.

01:37:41.130 --> 01:37:41.963
You know?

01:37:41.963 --> 01:37:45.440
And I think that that level
of autonomy is a blessing.

01:37:47.697 --> 01:37:51.490
It's not a guarantee to find
ourselves in this position.

01:37:51.490 --> 01:37:54.710
Well, I think I'm very grateful for that.

01:37:54.710 --> 01:37:56.997
So in a sense, when you say,

01:37:56.997 --> 01:38:00.014
"Well, you could play
a bass while DJ-ing,"

01:38:00.014 --> 01:38:02.673
it's like it's just a crazy
thing to be able to say.

01:38:02.673 --> 01:38:07.300
And, yeah, it's funny that you
said it but it's also true.

01:38:07.300 --> 01:38:09.130
It's like we're at a point in our lives

01:38:09.130 --> 01:38:13.960
where we do have the
freedom to pursue things

01:38:16.200 --> 01:38:21.200
and we don't really have
to get too much buy-in

01:38:21.740 --> 01:38:24.143
for things that we would wanna go after.

01:38:24.980 --> 01:38:26.180
Yeah.
You know?

01:38:26.180 --> 01:38:29.170
So it's really on us.

01:38:29.170 --> 01:38:31.610
We don't need to ask permission.

01:38:31.610 --> 01:38:33.313
We need to ask forgiveness.

01:38:33.313 --> 01:38:34.730
Well, you know,

01:38:35.610 --> 01:38:36.710
in an effort to wrap it up.

01:38:36.710 --> 01:38:41.337
I think that the way I've
been sort of framing it,

01:38:41.337 --> 01:38:44.640
and this is with the help of my therapist,

01:38:44.640 --> 01:38:48.113
is if you're a busy person,
and most people are busy,

01:38:49.760 --> 01:38:51.433
you kind of have to ask yourself,

01:38:52.867 --> 01:38:56.510
"Am I putting life giving
things onto my plate

01:38:56.510 --> 01:38:58.330
or life taking things onto my plate?

01:38:58.330 --> 01:39:01.420
And am I taking life taking
things off of my plate

01:39:01.420 --> 01:39:02.567
and then putting life
giving things on it?"

01:39:02.567 --> 01:39:04.400
And you know, as an individual,

01:39:04.400 --> 01:39:05.850
what those things are, right?

01:39:07.160 --> 01:39:10.060
Because even in a profession like ours,

01:39:10.060 --> 01:39:11.313
in which it's like, hey,

01:39:12.430 --> 01:39:15.850
it feels like it's all
fun and games to an extent

01:39:15.850 --> 01:39:17.400
because we do this...

01:39:17.400 --> 01:39:19.420
we're ridiculously lucky and fortunate

01:39:19.420 --> 01:39:20.667
to have the jobs that we have

01:39:20.667 --> 01:39:22.760
and to be able to do
the things that we do,

01:39:22.760 --> 01:39:24.620
but even we can still make decisions

01:39:24.620 --> 01:39:28.980
to put a bunch of life
taking things on our plate,

01:39:28.980 --> 01:39:30.540
the things that don't bring us joy,

01:39:30.540 --> 01:39:33.220
the things that seem obligatory,

01:39:33.220 --> 01:39:35.460
things that don't get
us into creative flow,

01:39:35.460 --> 01:39:37.540
whatever those things might be.

01:39:37.540 --> 01:39:42.100
And so I think going through
a list like this, to me,

01:39:42.100 --> 01:39:43.850
the things that I identified with

01:39:43.850 --> 01:39:45.670
in the majority of these people

01:39:45.670 --> 01:39:47.510
is what I would envision

01:39:47.510 --> 01:39:50.708
being a life giving thing to me, right?

01:39:50.708 --> 01:39:54.590
So it's a way to kind of evaluate...

01:39:54.590 --> 01:39:56.960
All right, again, we're
still very, very young,

01:39:56.960 --> 01:39:58.141
and like you said,

01:39:58.141 --> 01:40:01.283
there's so much opportunity
and there's so much freedom,

01:40:02.290 --> 01:40:04.270
but what kind of decisions
are you gonna make?

01:40:04.270 --> 01:40:07.040
Are you gonna make decisions
that are fear based,

01:40:07.040 --> 01:40:10.570
that are designed to
fulfill some obligation

01:40:10.570 --> 01:40:11.610
that you put on yourself

01:40:11.610 --> 01:40:13.770
or an obligation that you
think exists out there

01:40:13.770 --> 01:40:16.433
from someone, or are fans or whatever,

01:40:17.270 --> 01:40:18.920
or are you gonna make decisions

01:40:18.920 --> 01:40:23.920
to do things that give you life and joy

01:40:24.270 --> 01:40:26.623
and turn you into Rick Rubin in 20 years?

01:40:28.570 --> 01:40:29.440
Right?

01:40:29.440 --> 01:40:34.150
Like, what's your version
